# The build stamps the built file's REAL byte count and KB size into the landing
# page, so the bytes have to be the same everywhere or that number is a lie.
#
# They were not. On Windows with core.autocrlf=true the working tree is CRLF, so
# a local build produced 436,274 bytes and stamped "426 KB" onto the page, while
# the file GitHub Pages actually serves is the LF one at 433,199 bytes, 423 KB.
# The page advertised a size no user ever downloaded, and any CI rebuild
# disagreed with the committed artifact on those four lines forever.
#
# LF everywhere fixes both: the number on the page is the number people get, and
# a rebuild on Linux matches the commit byte for byte, which is what lets the
# stale-build check in .github/workflows/pr.yml mean anything.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched by any of that.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.stackdump binary
